AB  - The present study focuses on the implementation of artificial neural networks in the design and modeling of quadric surfaces for three-dimensional reconstruction. Artificial neural networks represent a promising tool in the field of computer vision and image processing, due to their ability to learn complex patterns and perform recognition tasks efficiently. In this work, a novel approach is proposed that uses neural networks to generate accurate models of quadric surfaces from three-dimensional input data. Training and optimization techniques are applied to tune the network parameters and achieve an accurate three-dimensional reconstruction. The results obtained show that the implementation of neural networks in the design and modeling of quadric surfaces significantly improves the quality and accuracy of three-dimensional reconstruction, which has important implications in fields such as virtual reality, robotics, and data visualization. reconstruction.
