AB  - While public speaking anxiety is prevalent, existing virtual reality (VR) training tools primarily focus on exposure rather than providing structured, performance-driven feedback. To address this gap, this research presents a comprehensive VR-based system that integrates immersive environments with real time speech and physiological analysis to enhance communication skills. The system utilizes Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) and Natural Language Processing (NLP) to evaluate semantic alignment, structural fidelity, and grammatical accuracy against prepared transcripts. Concurrently, a wearable-based subsystem monitors physiological signals to classify stress in real-time, triggering dynamic VR interventions such as breathing prompts and adaptive avatar behaviors. Additionally, a Speech Delivery Scoring (SDS) pipeline computes acoustic metrics to generate context-specific feedback on pace, clarity, and pitch. Finally, a Large Language Model (LLM) facilitates interactive Q&A sessions and generates personalized coaching strategies, offering a holistic approach to communication training beyond traditional exposure therapy.
ER  - 

