AB  - The world of higher education promotes the Education 5.0 paradigm where the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI), Virtual Reality (VR), and Multimodal Learning Analytics (MMLA) can be used to create humanfocused, technology-enhanced personalised learning experiences. In this study, the qualitative content analysis is performed on 16 peer-reviewed articles from 2019-2026 from Scopus database. Findings indicate a change in the behavioural surveillance to predictive modelling of affective states and neurocognitive load. Modular architectures using Large Language Models (LLMs) with Unity-based three- dimensional (3D) worlds are preferred technological trends. Infrastructure and biometric privacy are, however, the biggest obstacles. Finally, this study shows that longitudinal designs and humanAI collaboration models are necessary to overcome the institutional digital divide.
ER  - 

